---
title: Popovers
description: Tall, hollow popovers from a rested bread-flour batter, started hot and finished low.
tags: [bread, baking]
course: side
icons: [egg, wheat, oven]
source:
  name: Cook's Illustrated
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/1789-popovers
yield: 6%popovers
time: 2h30m
---

Adjust an oven rack to the lower-middle position and heat the oven to 450°F (230°C). Grease a 6-cup #popover pan{} with vegetable shortening, then dust lightly with flour.

Whisk the @large eggs{3} in a #medium bowl{} until light and foamy. Slowly whisk in the @low-fat milk{2%cup}(heated to 110°F) and @unsalted butter{3%tbsp}(melted and cooled slightly) until incorporated.

Combine the @bread flour{240%g}(2 cups), @salt{1%tsp}, and @sugar{1%tsp} in a #large bowl{}. Whisk three-quarters of the milk mixture into the flour mixture until no lumps remain, then whisk in the remaining milk mixture.

Transfer the batter to a large #measuring cup{}, cover with #plastic wrap{}, and let rest at room temperature for ~rest{1%hour}.

> **Making Ahead** — The batter can be refrigerated for 1 day. Bring it to room temperature before proceeding with the recipe.

Whisk the batter to recombine, then pour it into the prepared popover pan (the batter will not quite reach the top of the cups). Bake until just beginning to brown, about ~bake{20%minutes}.

Without opening the oven door, decrease the oven temperature to 300°F (150°C) and continue to bake until the popovers are golden brown all over, ~bake{35-40%minutes} longer.

Poke a small hole in the top of each popover with a #skewer{} and continue to bake until deep golden brown, about ~bake{10%minutes} longer.

Transfer the popover pan to a #wire rack{}. Poke again with the skewer and let cool for ~cool{2%minutes}. Turn the popovers out onto the wire rack. Serve.

> **Storing** — Once the popovers have cooled completely, they can be stored at room temperature in a zipper-lock bag for 2 days. To serve, adjust an oven rack to the middle position and heat the oven to 400°F (200°C). Heat the popovers on a rimmed baking sheet until crisp and heated through, 5 to 8 minutes.
